# Nohn Virtual World Law Layer — Global Economic Unified Standard V2.1
# Positioning: the "economic compliance details" among the four law-layer modules (identity attestation / communication protocol / physics baseline / compliance details).
# Core objective: virtual-world currency and real-world currency are 1:1 interoperable.

> This standard adopts a "real-world anchoring" model: anchored assets are pegged 1:1 to real reserves, while volatile assets are booked at real-time market value.
> This standard therefore does not adopt floating exchange rates; the original V2.0 clause "exchange rates are freely formed by the market, with no mandatory pricing" is repealed.

## 1. Asset Attestation
### 1.1 Real-World Asset Onboarding
#### A. Stable-Pegged
- [Compliant fiat stablecoins / CBDC]: mapped 1:1 against issuance reserves, integrated into the unified clearing and settlement path, and interoperable with all assets without discrimination.
- Mandatory Proof-of-Reserve (PoR): the issuer must provide an on-chain verifiable 1:1 reserve proof, verified in real time by the audit layer; a reserve ratio < 100% suspends redemption and triggers public disclosure.
- Redemption right: holders have the right to redeem anchored assets back into real fiat 1:1 at any time; the redemption channel must be permanent and may not be shut down by any single party (unconstitutional, see Constitution Art. 10).

#### B. Volatile Real-World Assets (no 1:1 promise)
- [Bitcoin / gold, etc.]: booked at the real-time fair value at the moment of onboarding, bound to a unique `nft_dna`; redeemed at real-time market value when leaving the world.
- Fixed-supply assets (e.g. BTC 21,000,000) are recorded only as on-chain mirrors and are not granted any "value-stable" property — their real-world price floats with the market.

### 1.2 Virtual World Assets
- [Platform currencies / points / tokens]: regardless of issuer or engine, once the "total issuance + circulation proof" is submitted they are automatically mapped to Nohn standard assets, with ownership bound to the user's `GlobalIdentity.soul_hash`, transferable, convertible, and storable across platforms.
- [NFTs / digital props / metaverse assets]: each generates a unique `ASSET_ID` recording "creator, attributes, history, permissions", with globally unique attestation; duplication is deemed invalid, completely eliminating counterfeiting and misappropriation.

## 2. Universal Value Swap
- Unit of account: `NOHN_POINT` (axiom point).
- Principles of real-world interoperability:
  - anchored assets → pegged 1:1 to real reserves;
  - volatile assets → converted into `NOHN_POINT` at real-time market value.
- Cross-world / cross-reality exchange: anchored assets follow the `1:1 value anchoring` principle, with no mandatory fees, no loss, instant settlement, and full traceability.
- Settlement cost: covered by reserve interest or protocol subsidy; unilateral charging of users is prohibited (consistent with Constitution Art. 10 "anti-centralized control", avoiding the introduction of centralized fee-collecting nodes).

## 3. Supply Control
- New issuance: a "value endorsement + purpose statement" must be submitted and pass audit before entering circulation, eliminating air coins and reckless issuance.
- Asset destruction: permanently recorded in the audit log and publicly disclosed network-wide; irrevocable.

## 4. Reserve Custody & Redemption
- Custodian: must be multi-sig / smart-contract custody subject to "on-chain Proof-of-Reserve (PoR) automated audit"; single-entity custodianship is prohibited.
- Redemption channel: holders of anchored assets may redeem real fiat 1:1 at any time; the redemption interface must be public and may not be unilaterally shut down.
- Bankruptcy isolation: reserve assets are isolated from the operator's assets; operator bankruptcy does not affect users' redemption rights.

## 5. Oracle & Valuation
- Assets valued at real-time market value must connect to ≥ 3 independent oracle sources, taking the median / weighted average to prevent single-point manipulation.
- Oracle signatures must be verifiable on-chain; abnormal volatility triggers a circuit breaker and manual review.

## 6. Asset Identifier Schema (for auditing and cross-world verification)
- `soul_hash`: SHA-256, 64 hexadecimal characters, bound to `GlobalIdentity` (see constitution_rules.py / Constitution Art. 6).
- `ASSET_ID`: format `ASSET-<chain>-<sha256(creator|timestamp|seq)>`, globally unique.
- `nft_dna`: on-chain asset fingerprint (e.g. BTC's `txid:index`), unforgeable and verifiable on-chain.

## 7. Frozen Asset Liquidation
- After identity freeze caused by permanent private-key loss (key-loss clause, see Identity Attestation Standard §1.1): all anchored assets of that soul are **permanently locked** — not destroyed, not transferred, not allocated to any public treasury.
- The corresponding real reserves remain locked; PoR stays at 100% (no reserve is ever released because of a freeze).
- The redemption channel closes permanently for that soul and must never be opened to any third party; assets and reserves stay sealed until the end of the world.
